Feature: Read-only narrow Memory support research
  Scenario: A controlled support diagnostic retains the production question
    Given a fixed reviewed authored corpus and an isolated empty agent directory
    When offline SDK transport captures the current production support request
    Then each case keeps the complete source state and unchanged support criteria
    And labels and case identities remain outside the model input
    And a separate accounting owner must provide any real transport
    And each real case uses one request with no SDK retry and stores its numeric response and usage
    And unavailable or wrong-model responses are incomplete cases rather than false holds
    And the diagnostic grants no threshold change, mutation authority or learning benefit

  Scenario: Fully cited new Memory retains complete independent checks
    Given original frozen citations privacy classification and complete evidence
    When a research judge uses Noul for body and description grounding
    Then support requires the original strong yes probability
    And speculation temporary faults unsupported scope and unresolved evidence remain held
    And counterevidence relationship and parent permission checks remain unchanged
    And no research judgment writes Memory or Harness

  Scenario: Every transformed request is checked before real inference
    Given a multi-window frozen dossier with a later oversized or sensitive request
    When a read-only fixture completes all preflight batches
    Then the entire research input is rejected before any external call
    And earlier successful fixture windows cannot authorize a partial review

  Scenario: Numeric observations preserve uncertainty without raw response text
    Given exact original question keys criteria and pinned model
    When a response contains valid Noul or Choice probabilities
    Then research records only controlled indexes labels and bounded numeric probabilities
    And malformed extra-key unknown-model or private-text answers produce no observation

  Scenario: A pinned semantic model cannot silently use another version
    Given Memory review requests an exact Jev model version
    When the service returns a different model version with positive answers
    Then the parent holds the review as an invalid response
    And actual model usage and known estimated cost remain recorded
    And explicitly moving aliases keep their configured version flexibility

  Scenario: Review consumers keep the parent model binding
    Given a parent judge requests a fixed supported Jev version
    When its complete or incomplete Memory review reaches a correction consumer
    Then the consumer requires the same requested and actual model version
    And old or foreign proofs cannot unlock correction fields
    And legacy injected judges retain the 1.13 version contract
    And each corrected candidate still requires complete fresh source and semantic review
